        "text": "How do traders and investors use market psychology? Assuming that the theory of market psychology is valid, understanding it may help a trader to enter and exit positions at more favorable times. The general attitude of the market is counterproductive. The moment of highest financial opportunity for a buyer usually comes when most people are hopeless and the market is very low. In contrast, the moment of highest financial risk often arises when the majority of the market participants are euphoric and and overconfident. Thus, some traders and investors try to read the sentiment of a market to spot the different stages of its psychological cycles. Ideally, they would use this information to buy when there is panic and sell when there is greed. In practice, though, recognizing these optimal points is rarely an easy task. What might seem like the bottom may fail to hold, leading to even lower bottom.",
